Next the most commonly encounter species are identified that cumulatively represent 50% of all recorded species records. This resulted in the selection of only four commonly recorded species, of which European hake was the most frequently encountered but following by other spp such as COE or OCC (Fig. 1).
```{r}
dat$prob = ifelse(dat$catchkg>0,1,0) # in case there are 0s
# Cumulative Species curve
spp = aggregate(prob~ sireno,dat,sum)
spp = spp[order(spp$prob,decreasing = T),]
# Cumulative distribution
spp$pcum = cumsum(spp$prob/sum(spp$prob))
spp$order = 1:nrow(spp)
spp$sireno = factor(spp$sireno,levels=unique(spp$sireno))
Figure 1 shows that four species cumulatively represent
